OK - I have seen the SAVOL2 oddity when you just take, I think,
methane and gradually shrink the CH distance from 1.09. At some
point, e.g. 1.081, there is a discontinuous drop in the SASA.

It definitely occurs for e.g. acetone where the HC sigma is the
smaller 2.42 rather than the usual 2.50. To avoid this in QikProp,
I always use 2.50 for any HC. Bill

----------------------------------------------------------------------
The standard probe radius for water in computing SASA 
is 1.4 A. This was used by Eisenberg (Nature 319, 199 (1986))
and I believe goes back to Lee & Richards, JMB 55, 379 (1971).
